  "prefLabel": "Bfa 506.01 CARRY FORWARD of Unused Bond Limit",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bfa 506.01 CARRY FORWARD of Unused Bond Limit. After the authority has reserved, assigned, or allocated bond limit to all private activity bonds to be issued in that calendar year, the authority shall carry forward unused bond limit under Section 146 of the Code. In determining which types of bonds shall receive a CARRY FORWARD of unused bond limit and the amount of that CARRY FORWARD, the authority shall apply the factors listed in Bfa 505.01.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Bfa 100) #5719, eff 10-13-93",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bfa100-500.html"
}
